---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../../../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="GridMetrics Support — Savoie Apps"
  description="Help, troubleshooting and contact details for GridMetrics."
  canonicalUrl="https://savoie.app/apps/gridmetrics/support/"
>
  <Navbar />
  <main class="app-info">
    <article class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">GridMetrics</p>
      <h1>Support</h1>
      <p class="lede">Need help with a forecast, tariff, widget, notification or GridMetrics Pro purchase? Email us and we’ll help you get it sorted.</p>

      <a class="contact" href="mailto:gridmetrics@savoie.app?subject=GridMetrics%20Support%20Request">Email GridMetrics support</a>

      <h2>Helpful details to include</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Your GridMetrics version and build number</li>
        <li>Your iPhone or iPad model and iOS version</li>
        <li>What you expected to happen and what happened instead</li>
        <li>A screenshot, if it helps explain the problem</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Common fixes</h2>
      <h3>The widget is not updating</h3>
      <p>Open GridMetrics to refresh the latest recommendation, then wait briefly for iOS to update the widget. If necessary, remove the widget and add it again.</p>

      <h3>Notifications are not arriving</h3>
      <p>Check that GridMetrics notifications are allowed in iOS Settings and that “Recommended window alert” is enabled in the app.</p>

      <h3>GridMetrics Pro is missing</h3>
      <p>Open Settings, choose “Explore GridMetrics Pro”, then use “Restore Purchases”. The one-time purchase is restored through the App Store account that bought it.</p>

      <h3>Forecasts or prices look unavailable</h3>
      <p>GridMetrics relies on public grid and tariff services. Check your internet connection and try again shortly; temporary upstream outages can delay fresh data.</p>

      <p class="footnote">GridMetrics does not offer emergency or real-time grid safety advice. For account, billing or supply issues, contact your electricity supplier.</p>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .app-info { padding: 4rem 0 5rem; }
  .app-info .container { max-width: 720px; }
  .eyebrow { margin: 0 0 .5rem; color: var(--color-primary); font-weight: 700; }
  h1 { margin: 0 0 1rem; font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 7vw, 3.75rem); letter-spacing: -.05em; }
  .lede { max-width: 42rem; color: var(--color-text-secondary); font-size: 1.12rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  .contact { display: inline-block; margin: 1rem 0 2rem; padding: .8rem 1rem; border-radius: .8rem; background: var(--color-primary); color: white; font-weight: 700; text-decoration: none; }
  h2 { margin: 2rem 0 .7rem; font-size: 1.3rem; }
  h3 { margin: 1.4rem 0 .35rem; font-size: 1rem; }
  p, li { line-height: 1.7; }
  li + li { margin-top: .35rem; }
  .footnote { margin-top: 2.5rem; padding-top: 1.25rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); color: var(--color-text-secondary); font-size: .9rem; }
</style>
